[s0l0!-header][h1]Defer[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

A [b]defer[/b] statement ensures that the function is called only after the surrounding function returns.

[s0l0!-header][b]For example:[/b][/s0l0!-header][code format="go" codeId="3326"]func welcome() {
    fmt.Println("Welcome")
}
func main() {
[b]  defer welcome()[/b]
  fmt.Println("Hey")
}[/code]
The code above will first output "Hey" and only after that output the result of the [b]welcome[/b]() function.
This happens because the call to [b]welcome()[/b] is deferred, meaning it waits until [b]main[/b]() finishes execution and only then calls it.
[note][b]defer[/b] is often used for cleanup, for example, to release resources used by the code, such as files, connections, etc.[/note]

