[s0l0!-header][h1]Multiple Defers[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

If you have deferred multiple function calls, they will execute in [b]last-in-first-out[/b] order.

[s0l0!-header][b]For example:[/b][/s0l0!-header][code format="go" codeId="3327"]func main() {
    fmt.Println("start")

    for i := 0; i < 5; i++ {
        defer fmt.Println(i)
    }

    fmt.Println("end")
}[/code]
[note]The defer calls are [b]stacked[/b] on top of each other, which is why they are executed in last-in-first-out order.[/note]

